   minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\\\\\\\\n  unfold minUpTo\\\\\\\\n  have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\\\\\\\\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\\\\\\\\n    exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\\\\\\\\n  have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\\\\\\\\n  generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\\\\\\\\n  rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\\\\\\\\n\n<truncated 40721 bytes>\nf)$. If $|V_2| = 1$, the degree requirement is satisfied. When $|V_2| \\\\\\\\ge 2$, `romanWeight(f)` is at least 4. If the graph radius is less than or equal to 3, the problem is resolved.\\\\n\\\\nThe failures with `k=1` in testing occurred when all vertices in $V_2$ had small degree, which coincides with radius being less or equal to 3. Specifically, in these cases, the graph is small ($n \\\\\\\\le 7$), and any graph with $n \\\\\\\\le 7$ has radius at most 3. If radius is at most 3, the radius plus one is at most 4, which is less or equal to the `romanWeight(f)`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n**Formalizing and Proving Inequality**\\\\n\\\\nIf the graph's radius is less than or equal to three, then the radius plus one is less than or equal to the Roman weight, provable by the `omega` tactic directly, because the roman weight is greater than or equal to four. Considering the case where the radius is greater than three, the goal is now to prove that the radius plus one is also less than or equal to the Roman weight. This can be addressed by testing a lemma `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_general`, within a test file.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n**Testing Automated Tactics and Definitions**\\\\n\\\\nAssessing if automated tactics can solve the `test_goal` theorem, specifically `omega` is insufficient due to not understanding graph theory definitions. The definitions of `radius`, `eccentricity`, `ballWithin`, `romanWeight`, and the Roman domination condition are now the focus. The lemmas `minUpTo_le`, `radius_le_eccentricity`, `two_le_romanWeight`, `radius_add_one_le_card`, and `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`, along with the core definitions, guide the direction of the proof.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"tool_calls\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"run_command\\\",\\\"args\\\":{\\\"CommandLine\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"ls -la /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/prover_eval\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"Cwd\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\\\":\\\"5000\\\",\\\"toolAction\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"Listing prover_eval directory\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"toolSummary\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"List prover_eval directory\\\\\\\"\\\"}}]}\"}","truncated_fields":["content"]}
